" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315977} {:answer/id #uuid "c3858021-49df-5890-b7d5-30813f99a2e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8554200b-b663-52a0-8e3d-3817e84aed0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315860} :answer-field/id #uuid "3230a8b4-805e-5348-a21b-273d105379f1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f5c097d-b8ef-5e78-80f1-563c7c1e4885" :question/math-academy-id "q-343879" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{″}-4y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼4+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that all the sine coefficients in the Fourier series of the particular solution are equal to zero.*\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}\\frac{n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}\\frac{n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{″}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation and have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})-4(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))=4+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n-4\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(-\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})=4+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2} &=4 \\\\ {a}_{n}(-\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-4) &=\\frac{2(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2} &=-1 \\\\ {a}_{n} &=\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+16)}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+16)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222040 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e42e65b-6e26-5a3f-9275-25a291e13138" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Resonant Harmonics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id 